{"name":"Tidewater","hex":"#c2e3dd","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tidewater","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A region in Virginia and Maryland, United States, along the coast and the Chesapeake Bay."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tidewater"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tidewater Region","blocks":[{"text":"Tidewater is a region in the Atlantic Plains of the United States located east of the Atlantic Seaboard fall line and north of the Deep South. The term \"tidewater\" can be applied to any region where water levels are affected by the tide. Still, culturally and historically, the Tidewater region refers most commonly to the low-lying plains of southeastern Virginia, eastern Maryland, the Eastern Shore, and the Chesapeake Bay. It can also encompass Delaware, the remainder of the Delmarva Peninsula, and northeastern North Carolina."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8a/Tidewater_region_painted_relief_map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tidewater_Region"},{"title":"Tidewater (marine services)","blocks":[{"text":"Tidewater, Inc. is a publicly traded international petroleum service company headquartered in Houston, Texas, U.S. It operates a fleet of ships, primarily providing vessels and marine services to the offshore petroleum and offshore wind industries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Garza_Tide107.JPG/330px-Garza_Tide107.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tidewater_(marine_services)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Powhatan_1880_historyofuniteds00wats_0086.jpg/500px-Powhatan_1880_historyofuniteds00wats_0086.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t